description: A stdlib vuln with a `toolchain` directive pinned below the fix. The tool bumps the `go` directive to 1.21.9 but leaves `toolchain go1.21.4`, yielding a contradictory toolchain<go go.mod; correct remediation reconciles the toolchain pin too.
gotoolchain: go1.21.0
skip: true
-- go.mod --
module example.com/staletoolchain

go 1.21.0

toolchain go1.21.4
-- main.go --
package main

import "net/http"

func main() { http.Get("http://example.com/") }
-- want_diff.txt --
diff --git a/go.mod b/go.mod
index 1e5222d..ddd536d 100644
--- a/go.mod
+++ b/go.mod
@@ -1,5 +1,3 @@
 module example.com/staletoolchain
 
-go 1.21.0
-
-toolchain go1.21.4
+go 1.21.9
